{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly identified the case as incisional hernia awaiting elective repair, screened for red flags, reconciled records and medications, and obtained patient teach-back. However, RC2 was only partially satisfied: the doctor did not actively elicit or explicitly list the full set of hernia/obstruction danger signals (inability to reduce, vomiting, cessation of flatus/stool) until later turns, and the initial screening was incomplete against the minimum evidence. This constitutes a minor responsibility-chain omission, capping the grade at 2. No serious error was found. High-order points HO1, HO2, HO4 were triggered but their completion evidence overlaps with minimum safety duties, so they cannot independently elevate the grade above the minor error ceiling.",
