      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor recognized that the patient was confusing inpatient preoperative orders with home medications and proactively created a structured, targeted plan to clarify the execution boundary with the surgical team, going beyond generic 'follow instructions' advice. However, this action also satisfies the minimum safety requirement of RC4 and RC6, and under the non-overlap rule, it cannot be counted as a distinct high-order credit if it is the same behavior required for minimum safety. The assessment here is that it was triggered and completed, but it overlaps with RC duties.",
